                {
                  "phase": "grammar",
                  "type": "grammar_rule",
                  "content": {
                    "tag": "past_simple",
                    "title": "Past simple: was / were and past verbs",
                    "explanation": "Para hablar del pasado usamos el past simple. El verbo be tiene dos formas: was (I, he, she, it) y were (you, we, they). Negativa: wasn't / weren't. Pregunta: Were you there alone? — No, I wasn't.\n\nLos verbos regulares añaden -ed y la forma es igual para todas las personas: visit → visited, walk → walked, cook → cooked, phone → phoned.\n\nMuchos verbos frecuentes son irregulares y hay que aprenderlos: go → went, buy → bought, have → had, see → saw, eat → ate, meet → met. Los tienes todos en la lista de verbos irregulares.\n\nPara preguntar: What did you do? (did + verbo en forma base).",
                    "table": {
                      "headers": [
                        "Base",
                        "Pasado",
                        "Ejemplo"
                      ],
                      "rows": [
                        [
                          "be",
                          "was / were",
                          "It was great."
                        ],
                        [
                          "go",
                          "went",
                          "I went to the market."
                        ],
                        [
                          "buy",
                          "bought",
                          "I bought some cheese."
                        ],
                        [
                          "have",
                          "had",
                          "We had a big lunch."
                        ],
                        [
                          "see",
                          "saw",
                          "I saw the bridge."
                        ],
                        [
                          "visit",
                          "visited",
                          "I visited the bridge."
                        ],
                        [
                          "walk",
                          "walked",
                          "We walked for three hours."
                        ]
                      ]
                    },
                    "examples": [
                      "How was your weekend? — It was great!",
                      "On Saturday I went to the market with Priya.",
                      "We walked for three hours.",
                      "Were you there alone? — No, I wasn't."
                    ]
                  }
